DEVIATIONS
==========

1. Differentiable D-calibration (Eq. 9).
   The training penalty in voicing/dcal.py assigns predicted-CIF values to bins
   with a temperature-softened membership (a softmax over squared distances to
   bin centres for events, a smoothed step for censored mass) so the term is
   differentiable, as Eq. (9) requires of an in-training loss. The
   evaluation-time D-calibration goodness-of-fit p-value in
   acoustics/calibration.py uses the standard hard binning with the Haider
   censored-mass spreading. The two agree in the hard-assignment limit.

2. Compute profile.
   The manuscript does not report a hardware profile. configs/experiment/main.yaml
   fixes an upper-bound profile (8x A100-80GB, fp32, effective batch 256,
   lr 2e-5, 800 epochs, ten seeds); see README and docs/PROVENANCE. No reduced
   quick-start default is provided; configs/experiment/_smoke.yaml exists only
   for the test suite.

3. ONNX export scope.
   workshop/export.py traces the gated-fusion and discrete-time hazard pathway
   given a Remnant-State vector and the clinical embedding. The sequential
   selective-scan encoder is left in PyTorch because the recurrence does not
   trace to a portable static graph.
